course: dictionary
lesson: 6093
title: Methodist: a church and its people
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A Methodist is a member of the Methodist Church, a Christian group that started in England. As an adjective, Methodist describes things that belong to this church, such as a Methodist chapel.
explain: «The Methodist Church was started by John and Charles Wesley in the 1700s; Charles wrote thousands of hymns.» The clues tell you that Methodism began with people, not with a place, and that it has songs (hymns) as part of its worship.
explain: «Protestant churches stress the Bible, faith and grace, and include Lutherans, Anglicans, Methodists, Baptists and Presbyterians.» This list shows that Methodists are one group among several Protestant churches. Use the list around a word to find its family.
fact: A Methodist is a member of the Methodist Church, a Christian group started in England.
fact: Methodism is a branch of Protestant Christianity.
fact: Methodists are known for hymn singing and for helping the poor.
fact: «The Methodist Church was started by John and Charles Wesley in the 1700s.»
fact: As an adjective, Methodist describes things: a Methodist chapel is a church building, and a Methodist school belongs to this church.
exercise: «The Methodist Church was started by John and Charles Wesley in the 1700s.» Who started the Methodist Church? | The Catholic Church | The Bible | *John and Charles Wesley | Methodist schools
exercise: Which phrase uses Methodist as an adjective, describing a thing? | a Methodist went home | *a Methodist chapel | two Methodists walked in | a Methodist sang loudly
exercise: Methodists are known for which activities? | Building castles | *Singing hymns and helping the poor | Running marathons | Painting pictures of the sea
test: «Charles wrote thousands of hymns.» What is a hymn most likely to be? | *A religious song | A kind of boat | A kind of bread | A school subject
test: Methodism is a branch of which kind of Christianity? | Catholic | *Protestant | Muslim | Jewish
exam: Sam says a Methodist is a kind of building. What is correct? | *A Methodist is a member of the Methodist Church | A Methodist is a kind of boat | A Methodist is a type of dance | A Methodist is a kind of building
